From c55123336c75146bb52c2668d95a8e1a389246d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 00:09:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3258/3799] soh: rename func_800AB9EC -> View_ApplyTo

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence HIGH) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: the flag-driven apply that writes into a caller-supplied display list rather than the context
Defined in soh/src/code/z_view.c.

Tagged [LLM:HIGH] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/include/functions.h    | 2 +-
 soh/src/code/speed_meter.c | 4 ++--
 soh/src/code/z_play.c      | 2 +-
 soh/src/code/z_view.c      | 3 ++-
 4 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/soh/include/functions.h b/soh/include/functions.h
index dc8db5ebb..b89823be2 100644
--- a/soh/include/functions.h
+++ b/soh/include/functions.h
@@ -1417,7 +1417,7 @@ s32 View_ApplyOrtho(View* view);  // was func_800AB0A8 [LLM:HIGH]
